meta {
  name: logout
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/logout/
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessTokenStudent}}
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required. The refresh token from login -- it gets blacklisted so it can
    // no longer be exchanged for new access tokens.
    // Omitting it returns 401 "Refresh token was not included in request data."
    // because JWT_AUTH_HTTPONLY is False, so there is no cookie to read it from.
    "refresh": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Blacklists the refresh token (`rest_framework_simplejwt.token_blacklist` is
  installed), so it cannot be used to mint new access tokens.

  The access token itself stays valid until it expires -- JWTs are not revocable
  -- so the frontend must also discard both tokens locally. With
  `JWT_AUTH_HTTPONLY = False` the frontend holds them, so that is its job.

  `GET` on this URL returns **405**; dj-rest-auth removed the GET form.

  ## API example response
  {
    "detail": "Successfully logged out."
  }
}
